# Changelog

Some notable changes to this project will be documented in this file. The full
changelog will be on the ANMS GitHub wiki: https://github.com/NASA-AMMOS/anms/wiki/ANMS-Changelog.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

## [Unreleased]

### Added
- Angular port of frontend UI, replacing Vue
- OpenSearch containers
- `/version` REST API
- Multi-file ADM upload and toast notification system
- Tag-based GHCR image publishing

### Changed
- PostgreSQL upgraded from v14 to v18
- ResourceCache replaced with LFU cache
- CI migrated to Podman v5
- Enterprise SSL certificate installation refactored
- Core routes consolidated and cleaned up
- Improved REST API error handling and SQL concurrency

### Fixed
- UID values exceeding SYS_UID_MAX
- ARI builder bugs

## [2.0.0] - 2025-10-30

### Added
- Light compose profile for reduced-footprint deployments
- GHCR container publishing pipeline
- Quickstart developer onboarding script
- SonarQube/SonarCloud CI integration
- Time-based and state-based rule creation in the build tab
- EDDS ARI selection on the build tab
- Grafana v12 with PostgreSQL internal database and text-provisioned dashboards
- Internal ARI transcoder, replacing external dependency
- Help page and 404 page handler

### Changed
- NGINX removed from the stack
- ION removed from ANMS images
- Podman support added alongside Docker
- ContainerFiles combined to eliminate intermediate images
- Core ARI translation and sending route consolidated
- Latest dtnma-tools and SQL schema adopted

### Fixed
- Correlator nonce misbehavior
- YANG file upload failures
- Transcoder log table navigation
- Overly permissive regex security issue
- Numerous CI stability and dependency upgrades

## [1.1.0] - 2024-08-26

### Added
- Agent details and management modals
- Received reports display with missing reports support
- Report generation and display in the build tab
- Navigation filtering on the exploration build tab
- GitLab CI pipeline

### Changed
- RHEL version updated for AMMOS compatibility
- ION switched to dtnma-tools backend
- Build script updated for image tar release

### Fixed
- Report database agent parameter handling
- ION hex string handling with blank spaces
- Rate limiter and code scanning issues
- Footer formatting overflow

## [1.0.0] - 2023-08-31

### Added
- Initial public release of ANMS v1.0, imported from private source repository

## [0.2.0] - 2022-06-10

### Added
- Build tab, which allows for building of ARIs
- anms-core, centralized orchestration component which now all ANMS-developed components will use to retrieve data from other components
- REST API documentation websites for anms-core in both OpenAPI (at /docs) and Redoc (at /redoc) formats
- Initial unit testing for anms-core and anms-ui
- All components now support PostgreSQL and MySQL databases, with notional support for MariaDB.

### Changed
- anms-ui now makes no direct db requests, they all are directed through anms-core
- Grafana now uses proxy authentication with nginx to secure all panels (visible inside of the monitor tab)
- Removed unsupported/non-functional UI components including Networking and Alerts tabs
- Fixed hard-coded and permanent admin and user accounts for UI, now only an admin is created on installation and can be disabled
- Fixed password complexity validation issues with UI
- Updated build.sh, configuration, and docker-compose files to support remote server deployment
- Updated Agents table and initial Agent pages to move away from use of Grafana for simple CRUD operations
- Removed incomplete user invitation system in lieu of server admin user account management
- Initial REST API role-based access controls for user management endpoint

## [0.1.1] - 2022-03-09

### Added
- Grafana panels and documentation for viewing report variables
- Interface to help construct controls that set up TBRs for agents to send reports at intervals

### Changed
- Updated versions of npm module dependencies per vulnerability analysis
- Fixed issues related to adding users

## [0.0.1] - 2022-02-08

### Added
- Initial Release
